What emerges
- Status: 99.0% of the movies are Released. The other statuses, empty included, add up to about 1%.
- Field completeness:
  - almost always present: title, date, imdb_id, poster (more than 99%);
  - then runtime 96%, genres 94.6%, languages 91.6%, production companies 73.9%;
  - budget known in only 19.5% of the movies, revenue in 16.3%, both in only 11.8%. The queries on money and earnings will work on about 5,000 movies.
- Dates: 53% of the movies were released from 2000 onwards. The oldest is from 1874.
- Genres: Drama is in 44.6% of the movies and Comedy in 29%. 5.4% have no genre.
- Languages:
  - English as the original language in 71%;
  - in 6.1% of the movies the original language is not among the spoken ones;
  - in 8.4% the spoken languages data is missing.
- Production countries: United States in 46.5% of the movies, then United Kingdom and France with about 9% each.
- Votes:
  - 49.6% of the movies have fewer than 10 votes;
  - only 2.5% have more than 1,000;
  - for movies with at least 10 votes the median is 6.3.
- Runtime: 76% of the movies last between 70 and 119 minutes. 4% have a runtime of 0 or missing.
- Collections: 9.9% of the movies are part of a saga. The largest in the dataset is The Bowery Boys with 29 movies; James Bond has 26.
